<title>USA: Fannie Mae to redeem $275 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae to redeem $275 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fannie Mae on Tuesday said that on June 27 it will redeem all outstanding amounts of four medium-term note issues totalling $275 million. The terms of the notes are as follows.</p>
<p>    Principal     Interest    Maturity	Cusip</p>
<p>     Amount	   Rate	  Date	  Number</p>
<p>   $100 million     7.00	04/24/01     31364CBS6</p>
<p>   $ 75 million     7.00	04/30/01     31364CCA4</p>
<p>   $ 50 million     7.00	04/24/01     31364CBP2</p>
<p>   $ 50 million     7.01	05/07/01     31364CCK2</p>
<p>The redemption price of the notes will be 100 percent of the principal amount plus interest accrued to the redemption date, Fannie Mae said.</p>
</text>
